---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "Mortgage Payment Affordability Checklist";
const description =
  "A practical checklist to validate mortgage affordability: payment components, DTI, buffers, and timing. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-22";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Affordability checklist</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Mortgage payment affordability checklist</h1>
    <p>
      Use this checklist to confirm your payment estimate is realistic before you commit to a home price or loan term.
      It focuses on cash flow, DTI, and common missing items.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="Affordability workflow review, DTI and buffer framing, and routing between payment math, PITI inputs, and stress-test decisions."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when affordability is the main decision</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when the question is not just payment math, but whether the payment still works after DTI, buffers, and stress tests.</li>
      <li>If you still need to build the payment itself, move next to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If the issue is really housing-payment components like PMI, taxes, and HOA, move next to <a href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">
      If you still need to build the payment itself, move next to how mortgage payments are calculated.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Mortgage payment inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount, note rate, and term.</li>
      <li>Taxes, insurance, HOA, and PMI assumptions.</li>
      <li>Escrow rules or reserves used by the lender.</li>
      <li>Time horizon if comparing scenarios.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">1) Confirm the full payment</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Principal and interest from the note rate and term.</li>
      <li>Property taxes and homeowners insurance (escrow).</li>
      <li>HOA dues and PMI if applicable.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">2) Check DTI impact</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use the full housing payment in the DTI calculator.</li>
      <li>Include all required monthly debt payments.</li>
      <li>Compare to the target ratio for your lender or program.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">3) Stress test the assumptions</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Test a higher tax or insurance amount.</li>
      <li>Test a slightly higher rate (0.25% to 0.50%).</li>
      <li>Test a smaller down payment if you are unsure.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">4) Compare payment vs total cost</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Lower payment can mean higher total interest if the term is longer.</li>
      <li>Use the amortization schedule to compare total interest at the same horizon.</li>
      <li>Keep loan amount and rate consistent when comparing terms.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">5) Budget for non-escrow costs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Maintenance and repairs (especially for older homes).</li>
      <li>Utilities that may be higher than rent.</li>
      <li>HOA special assessments or fees.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">6) Plan for changes</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Escrow adjustments, insurance renewals, and tax changes can increase monthly payments. Build a buffer so small changes do not
      force difficult trade-offs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Using a payment estimate that excludes taxes, insurance, HOA, or PMI.</li>
      <li>Ignoring DTI and relying only on lender pre-approval numbers.</li>
      <li>Assuming escrow will stay flat after closing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">How mortgage payments are calculated</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/dti-calculation-step-by-step">DTI calculation step by step</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should I include HOA and PMI in affordability?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. They are part of the required monthly housing payment and can significantly change DTI.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Why does my lender estimate change after closing?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Escrow adjustments and insurance renewals can change the payment even if the rate stays fixed.
    </p>
  </section>

    <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-a-debt-to-income-dti-ratio-en-1791/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          What is a debt-to-income (DTI) ratio?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Owning a home: mortgage basics
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

<section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Run the DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-22</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>




